<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#FFFFFF" />
    <base href="/" />
    @* No static <title> here: every page supplies its own through <PageTitle>, and with
       prerendering the HeadOutlet emits a real <title> element into this head. *@
    <meta name="description" content="bit Bink (Bit.Bink) - a Blazor-native drawing and ink library: pressure-aware strokes, brushes, erasers, selection, layers, annotations, undo/redo, collaboration and SVG/PNG export, with the engine written in C#." />

    @* Link previews: the card a chat client or a social site unfurls is the first impression a
       shared link makes. *@
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Bit.Bink" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Bink - drawing and ink for Blazor" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Signature fields, handwriting, whiteboards and annotation on one vector document model - with the ink engine written in C#, not a JavaScript drawing library." />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://bink.bitplatform.dev/icon-512.png" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />

    <ResourcePreloader />
    @* The site kit (app.css, theme.js, site.js - shared by every Utilities demo), then this demo's
       own sample styles. The canvas stylesheet (_content/Bit.Bink/bit-bink.css) is not linked here:
       Bit.Bink's JS initializer adds it to the page by itself. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["app.css"]" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["demo.css"]" />
    @* Scoped-CSS bundle: includes the client project's *.razor.css files as well. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["Bit.Bink.Demo.Server.styles.css"]" />
    @* Synchronous on purpose: applies the light/dark theme before first paint. *@
    <script src="@Assets["theme.js"]"></script>
    <ImportMap />
    <link rel="icon" href="favicon.ico" sizes="32x32" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="512x512" href="icon-512.png" />
    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="InteractiveWebAssembly" />
</head>

@* data-enhance-nav="false": a link followed before the WebAssembly runtime has started is a plain
   page load rather than an enhanced one. Enhanced navigation fetches and merges the next page while
   the runtime is still starting, and the router the runtime then attaches can render the address
   it read before the merge - the URL says /getting-started and the page is the landing page. Once
   the app is interactive its router handles every link itself and this attribute is not consulted. *@
<body data-enhance-nav="false">
    @* InteractiveWebAssembly rather than Auto or Server: BinkCanvas hands its command buffer to
       JavaScript without serializing it only on WebAssembly, and pointer input never waits on a
       network round trip there. The pages are still prerendered, so the first response carries them. *@
    <Routes @rendermode="InteractiveWebAssembly" />
    <div id="blazor-error-ui" data-nosnippet>
        An unhandled error has occurred.
        <a href="." class="reload">Reload</a>
        <span class="dismiss">&#128473;</span>
    </div>
    <script src="@Assets["_framework/blazor.web.js"]"></script>
    <script src="@Assets["site.js"]"></script>
</body>

</html>
